Video Four
- GitHub is a web-based repository hosting service.
- Other repository hosting services are Bitbucket, Azure Repos and Gitea.
- We can create a repository on GitHub by adding a name and description and selecting public or private.
- We can connect our GitHub repository to VS Code.
- git remote -v shows the remote repository URL.
- git remote add origin URL connects the local repository to GitHub.
- We can use git push to upload our code to GitHub.
- GitHub allows us to contribute to other people's projects.
- We can check their code, make changes and suggest improvements through pull requests.
- For private repositories, we need permission to access the code.